,title,link,text,language,family
0,Idoma people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Idoma_people,"The Idoma people are a West African ethnic group that primarily inhabit the lower western areas of Benue State, Nigeria. The bulk of their territory is inland, south of the Benue River, some seventy-two kilometers east of its confluence with the Niger River.",Idoma,Niger-Congo
1,Idoma people,https://grokipedia.com/page/Idoma_people,"The Idoma people's festivals, dances, and music function as communal rituals that reinforce historical narratives, celebrate prowess, and foster social cohesion, often commemorating agricultural successes or past conflicts.",Idoma,Niger-Congo
2,Idoma – TIPs,https://tips.translation.bible/tip_language/idu/,"Idoma (idu) is a(n) Atlantic-Congo language of Nigeria, marked as not endangered.The Hebrew in Genesis 27:13 that is translated into English as “curse” is translated in Idoma as “let the mouth that he throws on you catch me.” (Source: Andy Warren-Rothlin). See also curse.",Idoma,Niger-Congo
3,Idoma Traditional Songs | TikTok,https://www.tiktok.com/discover/idoma-traditional-songs,Explore the rich heritage of Idoma traditional songs and cultural music that celebrate the beauty of the Idoma tribe. Watch Tinubu dance to this Idoma song in the most entertaining video of the day. Enjoy lively Nigerian TikTok vibes! #dance #tinubu ...,Idoma,Niger-Congo
4,What Languages do People Speak in Nigeria?,https://worldpopulationreview.com/countries/nigeria/language,"It is from the Niger-Congo language family and has as many as 24 million native speakers, both within and outside of Nigeria. There are over 20 dialects of Igbo, but Umuahia and Owerri are considered to be the official dialects.",Idoma,Niger-Congo
5,Idoma Language Sample | Language Museum,https://www.language-museum.com/encyclopedia/i/idoma.php,"If you want to get a flavour of the Idoma language, check out a small sample at the Language Museum.He was not that Light, but was sent to bear witness of that Light. Statistics. Nigeria (600,000) - Total (600,000). Classification.",Idoma,Niger-Congo
6,Idoma Culture: A Look into Nigeria's Idoma People - Native Tribe Info,https://nativetribe.info/idoma-culture-a-look-into-nigerias-idoma-people/,"Idoma Language and Oral Traditions. The Idoma language, a member of the Benue-Congo family, is the primary language spoken. Dialects vary between communities, reflecting the regional diversity within the Idoma ethnic group. It’s a testament to their unique cultural identity.",Idoma,Niger-Congo
7,Idoma in Nigeria people group profile | Joshua Project,https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/12182/NI,"Learn about the Idoma in Nigeria people group. Profiles include statistics, text, photo, map, progress indicator and language resources.Their language belongs to the Idomoid cluster of the Volta–Niger (Niger–Congo) family.",Idoma,Niger-Congo
8,Idoma Origins & Festivals: Ritual and Revival,https://historicalnigeria.com/ancestral-echoes-idoma-origins-rituals-and-cultural-revival/,"The Idoma are an ethnic group of central Nigeria, located mainly in Benue State, with smaller populations in Kogi, Nasarawa, Taraba, and parts of Enugu.The Idoma language belongs to the Idomoid group within the Volta–Niger branch of the Niger–Congo family.",Idoma,Niger-Congo
9,"Lesson Note On Origin, Location And States Of Some Nigerian People...",https://www.headteacher.ng/origin-location-and-states-of-some-nigerian-people-for-primary-4/,This lesson on Some Nigerian People for Primary 4 discusses the origin of the people and their locations/states.Origin: The Idoma people are part of the larger Niger-Congo group of ethnicities.,Idoma,Niger-Congo
